// frontend.jsonc: the browser client: its decisions, the copies it keeps, and the requirements its model is held to (an area part: items whose id starts fe-, d-fe- or copy-browser-).
// A part of the Strata specification; spec.jsonc lists the parts. Generated by scripts/split-spec.mjs
// the first time, edited in place after that. See specifications/README.md.
{
  "decisions": [
    {"id":"d-fe-1","ref":"D-FE-1","title":"The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it.** Every view result the web application keeps is stamped with the tenant epoch, the generation and the erasure epoch the gateway read it at, one stamp for the whole reply. It is drawn as current only while its stamp is the newest the browser has heard and its last contact with the gateway is at most the contact bound old; otherwise it is drawn labelled with its age. A missing or evicted entry is a read from the gateway, never an error, and every write is decided again by the server."},
    {"id":"d-fe-2","ref":"D-FE-2","title":"Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content.** A service worker keeps only content named by its hash (the built files, the fonts, the parts of the tenant's interface definition) in the Cache API, and passes every other request through untouched; the bootstrapped page, which carries the session, is never stored, and a navigation falls back to a stored shell after a timeout. IndexedDB holds stamped view results, the write queue and drafts, encrypted per principal, with the known stamp beside them. The kernel worker's memory holds the hot set."},
    {"id":"d-fe-3","ref":"D-FE-3","title":"One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks and kept by a heartbeat","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks and kept by a heartbeat.** Each tab keeps its own kernel worker. The worker holding the exclusive lock of the site and principal opens the socket, drains the write queue and writes a heartbeat to IndexedDB; a follower that sees the heartbeat stop takes the lock over with a stealing request. The others hear notices on a BroadcastChannel and read the shared IndexedDB. A SharedWorker is not used: Chrome for Android re-enabled it only in 2026 and Samsung Internet does not support it. Idempotency keys keep a queued write applied once if two tabs ever both send it."},
    {"id":"d-fe-4","ref":"D-FE-4","title":"Custom elements draw, the kernel decides","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Custom elements draw, the kernel decides.** Web Components are renderers of the view model: they hold no application state, take properties, and report what the person did as events the main thread turns into kernel messages. They render into the light DOM so that labels, ARIA references and the page's styles reach them; a control with no native element is form-associated through ElementInternals. Declarative Shadow DOM is not used, because nothing is rendered on the server and no markup is parsed (D18)."},
    {"id":"d-fe-5","ref":"D-FE-5","title":"Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server.** A queued write holds the intent, the tenant epoch and record version it was decided on (none for a create) and an idempotency key drawn once its input is final and stored with it. A write that depends on another's result (an update of a record created offline, a reference to it) holds a local id and no key until that result is known. The leader sends each write with expected-epoch, expected-version and the key; the server commits it only at that stamp, and answers a repeat of the key with the recorded outcome. Queued writes carry a retention long enough for offline work, and the client never resends a key past that retention less a margin: it asks the person instead. A conflict is never merged silently: the person decides."},
    {"id":"d-fe-6","ref":"D-FE-6","title":"What cannot be done offline","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**What cannot be done offline.** Only an operation whose contract allows queueing may be queued; by default none does. Sign-in, step-up and anything needing a fresh authentication (D-700), payments and plan changes, roles, members, invitations, sessions, passkeys and second factors, schema changes and the Impact Lab, and subject rights requests are never queued: offline, their controls say they need a connection. Sign-out works offline: it deletes the browser's key and device id at once, so nothing left is readable, and tells the gateway on the next connection."},
    {"id":"d-fe-7","ref":"D-FE-7","title":"Data at rest is encrypted under a key held per enrolled device","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Data at rest is encrypted under a key held per enrolled device.** The identity service enrols a device for a principal, issues its device id, and keeps a random key share for it, sealed at rest, for a fixed lifetime from enrolment with rotation before it ends; it gives the share only to a session of that principal. The worker derives a non-extractable AES-GCM key from it and keeps it in memory; it persists the key only when the person keeps their work available offline on a device they mark as theirs, which a realm may forbid. This protects against the next user of the device and against a disk read after the key is gone; it does not protect against code running in the origin while the person is signed in."},
    {"id":"d-fe-8","ref":"D-FE-8","title":"An erasure epoch in every stamp, read before opening","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**An erasure epoch in every stamp, read before opening.** The browser holds opened values, so a key destruction (D-350), which raises no generation, would leave them current. The server raises a per-tenant erasure epoch in the transaction of every key destruction and sends it with every reply, notice and heartbeat; a read takes the epoch before, or atomically with, opening its sealed fields. On a new epoch the browser deletes every view result, every base value of a queued write and every prefilled draft value stamped with an older one, in the same transaction that raises its known epoch, and drops any later put of an older one."},
    {"id":"d-fe-9","ref":"D-FE-9","title":"No third-party code reaches the browser","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**No third-party code reaches the browser.** The QR code of an authenticator enrolment is drawn by an encoder of the web application's own, and the fonts are served from the site's own built files. Vite stays as the build tool; Playwright, axe and tsc stay as tools of development."},
    {"id":"d-fe-10","ref":"D-FE-10","title":"The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser.** A driver in Node runs the real kernel and the shell's view functions against the real gateway, interprets each uiScenario's steps against the drawn tree, and injects faults (lost replies, dropped sockets, reloads, a second tab) at the driver's boundary from a seed. Steps only a browser can answer (accessibility scans, cookies, screenshots, layout) run in Playwright."},
    {"id":"d-fe-11","ref":"D-FE-11","title":"Browser copies are reached at the next contact, within the session's idle lifetime","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Browser copies are reached at the next contact, within the session's idle lifetime.** The platform cannot reach a browser that is offline. A deletion, rectification, restriction, permission change or erasure reaches a browser copy at its next contact with the gateway; offline, the copy is drawn only labelled, and the session ends locally when the realm's idle lifetime (IDN-259, twelve hours by default) passes, which locks the copy. That is the erasure bound of the browser copy classes for CPY-013 and PRV-351. An erasure receipt (PRV-353) names the browser copy classes with that erasure point, and names a device that kept an offline key as reached at its next contact, with no bound."},
    {"id":"d-fe-12","ref":"D-FE-12","title":"A change the server cannot notify makes its views volatile","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**A change the server cannot notify makes its views volatile.** A notice names the keys that may differ since the previous frame on its connection. Where the server cannot know which views a change affects (a policy that reads the clock or follows references, a change published after a schema change), it marks the view volatile: every frame then names it, so it is current only between its own reply and the next frame. An out-of-commit change that alters what a principal may read sends a resync."}
  ],
  "copies": [
    {"id":"copy-browser-view","name":"Browser view result","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":12,"unit":"hour","mechanism":"stamped with the tenant epoch, generation and erasure epoch of its reply; drawn as current only at the newest stamp heard and within the contact bound of the last contact, carried forward by notices, and otherwise drawn labelled with its age; while offline, at most until the session would end unused, which a realm may shorten (IDN-259)","source":"d-fe-1"},"erasure":{"point":"the next contact with the gateway (a new erasure epoch, a membership or restriction notice, a deleted share), or the end of the session's idle lifetime, which locks it; a device that kept an offline key is reached at its next contact, with no bound","bound":12,"unit":"hour","source":"d-fe-11"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"View results kept in IndexedDB by the web application, per site and principal, encrypted under the key of the enrolled device (D-FE-7). Correctness never depends on it (D-FE-1)."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-queue","name":"Browser write queue","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":7,"unit":"day","mechanism":"a queued intent with its key and decided stamp, removed when the gateway answers it; never resent past its key's retention less a margin (D-FE-5); base values of other records are deleted on a new erasure epoch or a membership change (D-FE-8)","source":"d-fe-5"},"erasure":{"point":"the gateway's answer, sign-out on the device, or deletion of the device's share (sign-out everywhere, the device revoked, the principal removed or erased, the end of the share's lifetime), which makes it unreadable","bound":14,"unit":"day","source":"d-fe-7"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"Writes the person made while offline, kept in IndexedDB encrypted under the key of the enrolled device until the leader tab has sent them and the gateway has answered."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-interface","name":"Browser interface definition","of":["tbl-schema-history"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"each part is named by the hash of its content, so a changed part is a new entry; the manifest is read again on every schema notice","source":"d-8250"},"erasure":{"point":"dropped when the manifest no longer lists it, or when the browser evicts the site's storage"},"description":"The parts of the tenant's interface definition, kept by the service worker in the Cache API. They hold no personal field and no record data (D-8250)."}
  ],
  "claims": [
    {"id":"fe-001","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, in every schedule whose frames name every held key that may have changed, an answer returned as current SHALL be the server's opened value at the generation and erasure epoch the client last heard.","rationale":"Completeness of notices is the server's obligation; given it, a current answer is exactly what the server held at the stamp the client knows.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::current_value","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::run_coh"],"ref":"FE-001","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","d-fe-12","g-19","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-009","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, a cached value that is not returned as current SHALL be returned labelled with the generation it was read at.","rationale":"Offline and while catching up, an older copy is still useful to read, as long as it says how old it is.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_stale_older"],"ref":"FE-009","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-002","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, a commit receipt read at the server's current stamp SHALL make the next read of the written key return the committed value as current.","rationale":"A person who saves sees what they saved, not an older copy.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_after_commit","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::receipt_read"],"ref":"FE-002","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-003","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, every commit and every key destruction that an answer returned as current does not reflect SHALL have begun within the contact bound before the read.","rationale":"The browser's knowledge lags; the contact bound is what limits the lag, with no assumption on notices.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::current_recent"],"ref":"FE-003","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","d-fe-8","d-350","g-350"]},
    {"id":"fe-012","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, every entry at rest SHALL carry the erasure epoch the client has heard, which after a contact is the server's.","rationale":"A late reply or another tab's put of an older epoch must not write erased plaintext back after a purge.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::rest_one_epoch","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::contact_purges"],"ref":"FE-012","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-8","d-350","g-350"]},
    {"id":"fe-004","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, a value kept at rest for one principal SHALL open with no key the browser holds for another principal.","rationale":"Separation on a shared device rests on which keys are present, not on which partition the code chooses to open.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::no_cross_principal","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::served_own"],"ref":"FE-004","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.Opens`","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-005","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a principal signs out, with or without a connection, no value the principal left at rest SHALL open with any key the browser then or later holds.","rationale":"Sign-out on a shared device must leave nothing readable, even when deleting the stored data did not complete or the gateway never heard of it.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::signout_erases","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::offline_signout_erases"],"ref":"FE-005","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (signOut, signOutOffline)","traces":["d-fe-6","d-fe-7","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-006","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a session ends, a value its principal left at rest SHALL open only after a session of that same principal fetches its device's key share again.","rationale":"Queued work survives an expired session for its own author and for no one else.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::expire_locks","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::unlock_needs_own_session"],"ref":"FE-006","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (expire, fetchKey)","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-007","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a first submission of a queued write SHALL commit only when the kernel allows it and, for a write with a stamp, the tenant is at the expected epoch and the record at the expected version.","rationale":"A write decided offline on an old copy must not overwrite a change it never saw, and a restore must not make an old version match.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_ok_guard","lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_classes"],"ref":"FE-007","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-010","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a submission of a queued write that does not commit SHALL leave every record, its version and its value unchanged.","rationale":"A conflict, a refusal and a repeated key are reported to the person and change nothing.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_not_ok_unchanged"],"ref":"FE-010","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-008","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, in every schedule in which the server keeps each committed key for the retention and the client sends each key only within the retention of first sending it, a queued write SHALL be applied at most once.","rationale":"Reloads, lost replies and a second tab resend queued writes; each must take effect once, which rests on two local rules, one for each side.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-008","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-fe-3","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-011","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a queued write carrying the tenant epoch and the record version SHALL be applied at most once, whatever keys the server forgets and whatever restores occur.","rationale":"An update or delete decided on an epoch and version cannot apply twice, because its first application moves the record off that stamp for good and a restore moves the tenant to a new epoch.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::stamped_at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-011","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"]}
  ]
}
